---
// Why an LLM backtest can leak: the model's training text overlaps the backtest window (Glasserman and Lin, arXiv 2309.17322).
// Dates below are an example: say a model's training text ends in mid-2024.
const W = 900, H = 330;
const L = 190, R = 860, y0 = 2018, y1 = 2026;
const X = (y: number) => L + ((y - y0) / (y1 - y0)) * (R - L);
const cutoff = 2024.5;
---
<figure class="p22a">
  <div class="p22a-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Timeline from 2018 to 2026. A model's training text runs to mid-2024. A backtest over 2022 to 2023 lies inside that window, so the model may already know what happened next. A test from mid-2024 onward lies after the cutoff and is a fair test.">
      <text x="20" y="28" class="h"><tspan data-lang-en>An LLM may have read the answer before you ask it the question</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>LLM có thể đã đọc đáp án trước khi bạn hỏi</tspan></text>
      {[2018, 2020, 2022, 2024, 2026].map((y) => (
        <g>
          <line x1={X(y)} x2={X(y)} y1="56" y2="262" class="grid" />
          <text x={X(y)} y="286" text-anchor="middle" class="tick">{y}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="20" y="92" class="t"><tspan data-lang-en>Model's training text</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Văn bản huấn luyện</tspan></text>
      <rect x={X(2018)} y="72" width={X(cutoff) - X(2018)} height="30" rx="4" class="bar" />
      <text x={X(cutoff) - 8} y="92" text-anchor="end" class="in"><tspan data-lang-en>reads everything up to the cutoff</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>đọc mọi thứ đến mốc cắt</tspan></text>
      <text x="20" y="152" class="t"><tspan data-lang-en>Backtest on 2022-2023</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Backtest 2022-2023</tspan></text>
      <rect x={X(2022)} y="132" width={X(2024) - X(2022)} height="30" rx="4" class="bar bad" />
      <text x={X(2024)} y="186" text-anchor="end" class="n red-t"><tspan data-lang-en>inside the window: it may know the ending</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>trong cửa sổ: mô hình có thể đã biết kết cục</tspan></text>
      <text x="20" y="212" class="t"><tspan data-lang-en>Test from mid-2024</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Kiểm tra từ giữa 2024</tspan></text>
      <rect x={X(cutoff)} y="192" width={X(2026) - X(cutoff)} height="30" rx="4" class="bar ok" />
      <text x={X(cutoff) - 8} y="212" text-anchor="end" class="n gold-t"><tspan data-lang-en>after the cutoff: a fair test</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>sau mốc cắt: phép thử công bằng</tspan></text>
      <line x1={X(cutoff)} x2={X(cutoff)} y1="56" y2="262" class="cut" />
      <text x={X(cutoff)} y="50" text-anchor="middle" class="n"><tspan data-lang-en>training cutoff (example)</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>mốc cắt huấn luyện (ví dụ)</tspan></text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Say a model's training text ends in mid-2024. Glasserman and Lin tested this with headlines: removing company names made the in-window results better, not worse.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Giả sử văn bản huấn luyện của một mô hình dừng ở giữa 2024. Glasserman và Lin thử với tiêu đề tin: bỏ tên công ty đi thì kết quả trong cửa sổ tốt hơn, chứ không kém đi.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .p22a { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .p22a-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .p22a svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .h { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .t { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .n { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .in { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--bg); font-weight: 700; }
  .tick { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .red-t { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .gold-t { fill: var(--gold-icon); font-weight: 700; }
  .grid { stroke: var(--border); }
  .cut { stroke: var(--text); stroke-dasharray: 5 4; stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .bar { fill: var(--text-faint); }
  .bar.bad { fill: var(--red); opacity: 0.85; }
  .bar.ok { fill: var(--gold); }
  .p22a figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
